# .gitignore is a WHITELIST, not a blacklist.
#
# A denylist can only enumerate what somebody already thought of: every new file
# that appears in the tree is staged by default, so one slipped into a commit
# unnoticed. This inverts the default — ignore everything, then re-admit only
# what this repository is supposed to ship.
#
# Shape, in three layers:
#   1. /*              ignore every root entry, so nothing new is admitted by default
#   2. !/<path>        re-admit a shipped root file or directory
#   3. per-directory   inside each admitted directory, ignore its contents and
#                      re-admit the exact file patterns
#
# Layer 3 is not optional. Re-admitting a directory with `!/personas/` is not
# enough: git then descends into it and finds no further rule, so ANY file
# dropped there is admitted. That was measured on this repository, not assumed.
#
# Ordering matters and gitignore has one sharp edge: an excluded *directory*
# cannot have its contents re-included. So a directory that must ship its
# contents is re-admitted with a trailing slash (`!/skills/*/`) BEFORE the rule
# that excludes what is inside it.
#
# What this makes machine-checkable, with no memory required: the third-party
# skills, the private data directories of a retired lineage, the profile wiring,
# and this repository's own runtime state are excluded by the default rather than
# by remembering to exclude them. Their names are not listed here on purpose —
# see tools/leak-needles.local.txt for why.

# --- 1. default: ignore everything at the repository root ------------------
/*

# --- 2. re-admit the published root files ----------------------------------
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/README.zh.md
!/README.zh.md
!/cordis.patch.yml
!/install.sh
!/package.json

# --- 2. re-admit the preset's own plugin modules (shipped at the root) ------
!/lane-composition.mjs
!/plan-aware-persona.mjs
!/routing-sections.mjs

# --- personas/ ---
!/personas/
!/personas/
/personas/*
!/personas/analyst.md
!/personas/archivist.md
!/personas/auditor.md
!/personas/forge.md
!/personas/orchestrator.md
!/personas/planner.md
!/personas/reader.md
!/personas/scout.md
!/personas/seer.md
!/personas/wright.md

# --- tools/ ---
!/tools/
!/tools/
/tools/*
!/tools/audit-personas.mjs
!/tools/verify-install.sh
!/tools/gen-cordis-patch.mjs
!/tools/preset-declaration.mjs

# --- skills/ ---
!/skills/
!/skills/
/skills/*
!/skills/orch-delegation-brief/
/skills/orch-delegation-brief/*
!/skills/orch-evidence-protocol/
/skills/orch-evidence-protocol/*
!/skills/orch-real-path-testing/
/skills/orch-real-path-testing/*
!/skills/orch-discussion-protocol/
/skills/orch-discussion-protocol/*
!/skills/orch-delegation-brief/SKILL.md
!/skills/orch-discussion-protocol/SKILL.md
!/skills/orch-evidence-protocol/SKILL.md
!/skills/orch-real-path-testing/SKILL.md

# --- plugins/ is NOT distributed ------------------------------------------
# This repository used to ship a companion plugin here. Everything it did now
# lives in extensions/dsh/aegis-prefix.js, as one plugin doing both jobs in a
# single registration pass — which is what removed the race between them. There
# is deliberately no `!` rule for plugins/; do not add one back, and do not
# reinstate the plugin, because shipping both would reproduce that race in every
# installing deployment.

# --- extensions/ — the bundle's own plugins --------------------------------
# Both files are mounted by patch rows the generator emits and are resolved
# through the package specifier, so each must also appear in package.json's
# exports map. Listed one by one rather than as extensions/dsh/*.js: a plugin
# added later should fail LOUDLY here rather than slip into the published tree,
# which is the same default-deny reasoning as the `/*` above.
!/extensions/
/extensions/*
!/extensions/dsh/
/extensions/dsh/*
!/extensions/dsh/index.js
!/extensions/dsh/aegis-prefix.js

# --- docs/ is NOT distributed --------------------------------------------
# The four design documents stay on disk for the author and are held out of the
# published tree by the `/*` default above — there is deliberately no `!` rule
# re-admitting them. Do not add one. They are large internal history, not part
# of the installable preset, and the README says so rather than linking to them.

# --- 4. what the default already excludes (documented, not enumerated) ------
# node_modules/                install output and pnpm links
# .dsh/                        this repo's own evidence + state (runtime only)
# .install-tmp/ .clonetest/    install and clone-test scratch
# profiles/ presets/           the live host's wiring, applied to a DSH home
# example.zh/                  the Chinese personas are NOT shipped; see README.zh.md
# any other skills/*/          third-party skills are not redistributable here.
#                              NOT enumerated on purpose: what is installed on a
#                              given machine is that person's environment, not this
#                              project's, and some of it carries no licence at all.
#                              Enforcement is `/*` above, which refuses everything
#                              not explicitly re-admitted.
# retired-lineage data dirs/    private, and not named for the same reason
# tools/leak-needles.local.txt  this machine's own denylist; see that file's header
# *.bak *.bak-*                stray backups

# --- 5. binary assets, if any are added later ------------------------------
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
